From 5b078e17658536ccc7570351a3ab3279c299a759 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikita Sokolsky <sokolx@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 20:19:02 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] shader: slim texture classes in MSL before the library
 compile

The Metal compiler instantiates every member of a texture class the first time a source
names the type (409 member functions for texture2d<float> at MSL 4.0, about 40 ms per type
per library). Give each library its own explicit specializations with only the methods it
calls, read from the installed standard library headers. A library that does not compile
with them is compiled as generated. MVK_P60_NO_SLIM_TEXTURES=1 turns the pass off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKShaderModule.mm    |  44 +-
 .../Utility/MVKSlimTextureClasses.cpp         | 375 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../MoltenVK/Utility/MVKSlimTextureClasses.h  |  40 ++
 3 files changed, 458 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 MoltenVK/MoltenVK/Utility/MVKSlimTextureClasses.cpp
 create mode 100644 MoltenVK/MoltenVK/Utility/MVKSlimTextureClasses.h

